  "summary": "Malicious code in lynxog (npm)",
  "details": "The package's main entry point (main.js) is a heavily obfuscated JavaScript payload, alongside a second 1.1MB obfuscated file (Levvi.js). It declares a dependency on the WhatsApp library @whiskeysockets/baileys but aliases it to npm:levvleys, so installing the package pulls in an attacker-controlled substitute for the real library that the bundled bot code imports. A functional WhatsApp bot module (lynx/index.mjs) is shipped alongside the obfuscated payloads.",
